@startuml
title Run Out of Stage Time

hide footbox

legend top right
  |<#E6E6E6> View (React / TypeScript) |
  |<#CFE3F7> Controller (Java) |
  |<#D8F0D8> Model (Java) |
endlegend
autonumber

skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor LightCyan
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActorBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam ArrowColor SlateGray
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor SlateGray
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor LightYellow
    BorderColor Orange
}


' ==========================================
' Participants, coloured by MVC layer as in "Explode Bomb" (see legend).
' The stage timer is part of the third step of stage.update(), just
' before the enemies move. Includes "Spawn Enemy Wave" (10 Pontans).
' ==========================================
actor "Time" as time

participant "GameLoop" as view #E6E6E6

participant "GameBridge" as bridge #CFE3F7

participant "game : Game" as game #D8F0D8
participant "stage : Stage" as stage #D8F0D8
participant "EnemyFactory" as factory #D8F0D8
participant "pontan : Enemy" as pontan #D8F0D8

time -> view : next animation frame
view -> bridge : tick(inputMask)
bridge -> game : update(input)
game -> stage : update(input)

note over stage, factory
  Order of stage.update(): 1. the player ("Move Bomberman", then
  "Place Bomb" and "Detonate Bomb Remotely"), 2. bombs ("Explode
  Bomb"), 3. the stage timer (this diagram) and enemies ("Move
  Enemies"). The timer runs only while the stage runs (PLAYING or
  DYING), not while paused or on the "STAGE n" screen.
end note

opt timeLeft > 0
    stage -> stage : timeLeft--
    note right of stage
      Counted in ticks: 200 game seconds,
      each about 1.55 real seconds (93 ticks).
      The view shows timeLeft in game seconds.
    end note

    opt timeLeft reached 0
        stage -> stage : enemies.clear()
        note right of stage
          All enemies vanish at once, including
          dying ones. No points for them.
        end note

        loop 10 times
            stage -> factory : create(PONTAN, random spawn cell)
            create pontan
            factory -> pontan : new Enemy(PONTAN type, Pursuer strategy, cell)
            factory --> stage : pontan
            stage -> stage : enemies.add(pontan)
        end
        note right of factory
          Spawn Enemy Wave. A spawn cell is any random
          cell with no block, bomb or lingering flame,
          except the player's own cell. There is no
          safe distance, so a Pontan can appear right
          next to the player. Pontan is fast (1.0 px
          per tick) and passes soft blocks, as in
          "Move Enemies".
        end note
    end
end

note over stage, pontan
  This happens only once per stage: timeLeft stays at 0.
  Play continues; the door still needs noEnemiesLeft(),
  so all Pontans must be killed first. Waves still pending
  from a bombed door or power-up spawn nobody, because the
  stage already holds 10 living enemies.
end note

stage --> game
game --> bridge
bridge --> view
note over view, bridge : The frame is then drawn as in\n"Explode Bomb" (getState, draw, sounds).

@enduml
